0..69 Comment "// The shape of a category, after the HoTT book\'s Definition 9.1.1 (a"
70..142 Comment "// precategory): objects, a hom-type between two of them, identities and"
143..217 Comment "// composition with the unit and associativity laws as rules. Its model in"
218..288 Comment "// types and functions meets every law by conversion, and a law may be"
289..331 Comment "// proved by another law of the same type."
333..406 Comment "/// The category shape: a sort of morphisms dependent on the objects. Its"
407..486 Comment "/// laws over the dependent sort nest an operation the cell layer does not read"
487..505 Comment "/// there (#1510)."
